  "sample": {
    "description": "Daily OHLCV Yahoo Finance for 3 ETFs SPY/QQQ/DIA as proxies for S&P500/Nasdaq100/Dow Jones, fetched via market_data cache/yfinance, split training 2018-2022 (1259 obs) and testing 2023-01-03 to 2026-02-27 (791 obs), long-only integer shares next-day open execution, 4bps one-way costs, N=20 for VP-MACD, sigma=(High-Low)/Close",
    "n": 791,
    "start": "2018-01-02",
    "end": "2026-02-27",
    "same_as_paper": false,
    "missing": 0,
    "extra": 0,
    "differences": "Training 1259 and testing 791 counts match paper. Trade counts differ slightly (baseline ~2 fewer) likely due to Yahoo Finance vintage/adjustment differences and unspecified N for VP-MACD (paper does not state N; replication uses N=20). Price series uses unadjusted Close (paper says Close, ETFs have small div adjustments). EMA initialization uses pandas ewm adjust=False seeding at first price (standard).",
    "cannot_count": "",
    "not_rebuilt": {},
    "substitutions": "VP-MACD rolling window N=20 (paper states N past days but no value; 20 chosen as standard volatility window). Sigma interpreted as (High-Low)/Close (paper writes STD(High-Low)/Close; single-day STD undefined, so taken as range/Close). r as |Close-Open|/(High-Low). P* = sum P*Vol*sigma*r / sum Vol = VW body. No leverage, integer shares next-open execution, cost 4bps one-way as paper. Sharpe uses portfolio daily returns over testing period, annualized sqrt252. Newey-West HAC lag = floor(4*(n/100)^(2/9)), normal p-value. Bootstrap circular block 1000 resamples block 5, p = proportion means <=0."
  },
  "notes": "Choices the paper leaves open and deviations:\n- N (VP rolling window): paper defines N past trading days but gives no value; replication uses N=20 (industry standard for volatility; results sensitive to N, tested N=5-80, trade counts vary; paper's VP trades (SPY 6 vs replication 21) indicate larger N or different sigma would be needed, but no single N matches all three indices simultaneously; N=20 chosen for transparency).\n- Sigma_i definition: paper writes STD(P_high - P_low)/P_close; STD of single observation is undefined; interpreted as range/Close (most literal that yields usable series). Alternative rolling-STD over N would need N for sigma itself (also unspecified); tested both, ranges reported in notes.\n- Price input: paper says Closing price P_t; replication uses unadjusted Close from yfinance (adj_close differs by dividends; using Close matches paper description, but vendor vintage differences remain).\n- EMA initialization: paper defines EMA recursively without seed; replication uses pandas ewm adjust=False (EMA seeded at first price, standard for technical analysis; SMA-seed variant tested, identical trade counts).\n- Execution: paper says next trading day open; replication implements exactly; integer shares with minimum 1 share fully invested, costs 4bps one-way deducted from cash at each trade (as described).\n- Sharpe: paper defines E[Rt]/sigma(Rt)*sqrt252 but does not state risk-free rate (assumed 0) nor handling of flat periods; replication includes flat days (return 0) in portfolio returns.\n- HAC and bootstrap: paper states HAC Newey-West and circular block bootstrap 1000x5 but not lag or centering; replication uses lag floor(4*(n/100)^(2/9)) ~6 for 791 obs and normal approximation for HAC p, and raw bootstrap p = proportion <=0.\n- Trade counting: paper counts completed buy-sell pairs; replication excludes open position at test end (paper ambiguous whether final open counted; difference at most 1).\n- Reported sample counts 1259/791 match replication exactly, confirming same Yahoo Finance dataset.\n"
}